---
import { E } from "@/components/ui/e";
import { R } from "@/components/ui/r";

import BoxContent from "@/components/ui/box-content.astro";
import BoxHeader from "@/components/ui/box-header.astro";
import Box from "@/components/ui/box-index.astro";
import BoxTitle from "@/components/ui/box-title.astro";
---

<Box>
    <BoxHeader>
        <BoxTitle>Computer Programming</BoxTitle>
    </BoxHeader>
    <BoxContent>
        <div class="text-sm leading-7 font-medium">
            I started programming after <b>10th grade</b> with <b>C</b>. Then I began solving problems regularly on
            online judges such as
            <E href="https://codeforces.com/">Codeforces</E>,<E href="https://lightoj.com/">LightOJ</E>, and
            <E href="https://leetcode.com">LeetCode</E>. Over that time, I solved <b>1,000+ unique problems</b> across
            these platforms. You can find my solutions at the link below:
            <br />
            <R href="https://github.com/mt-shihab26/problem_library">Problem Library</R>
            <br />
            <br />
            Along with <b>problem-solving</b>, I studied <b>data structures</b> and
            <b>algorithms</b>, and applied that knowledge to solve problems. You can find my implementations of data
            structures and algorithms at the link below:
            <br />
            <R href="https://github.com/mt-shihab26/dsa_library">DSA Library</R>
            <br />
            <br />I also regularly read <i>programming-related books</i>. You can find the
            <b>source code</b>, <b>practice exercises</b>, and <b>notes</b> from those books as Markdown files at the
            link below:
            <br />
            <R href="https://github.com/mt-shihab26/books">Books Library</R>
            <br />
            <br />
        </div>
    </BoxContent>
</Box>
